# VM sparse-checkout patterns (non-cone, gitignore syntax) — VM-SPARSE-SYNC, 2026-11-02.
#
# Applied by scripts/deploy_pull_restart.sh on EVERY sync (ict-git-sync timer +
# the pull-and-deploy system-action), read from origin/main AFTER the fetch, so
# a change here reaches the VM on the next tick without any manual step.
#
# Why: #22365 put 21.6 GB of research caches (comms/research/<unit>/<run>/
# streams/*.pkl, work/) on main; the VM's `git reset --hard origin/main`
# checked them out and filled the 45G root disk -> the web API went blind.
#
# Rule: exclude ONLY bulk research artefacts that nothing on the VM reads.
# Verified 2026-11-02 by grep over src/, scripts/ops/, scripts/*.py|sh and
# config/ (every ExecStart in deploy/*.service): the runtime reads JSON / JSONL /
# MD under comms/research (verdict.json pointers in config/*.yaml,
# profile_loader's bybit-fee-measured json, mandate_resolver, soak_book_grade,
# attention_watch, research catalog) — those all STAY. Nothing on the VM opens a
# .pkl/.npz/.csv/.parquet under comms/research or a streams/ work/ candles/ dir.
# Adding a VM reader of an excluded shape means removing its line here first
# (tests/test_vm_sparse_checkout.py pins the runtime paths that must stay).
#
# The last matching line wins; `/*` = everything, `!` lines exclude.
